{
  "info": {
    "name": "pgfoundation (FastAPI)",
    "description": "PostgreSQL Database Foundation Server.\n\n**Generated** from the live OpenAPI document by `curls/generate.py` \u2014 do not edit by hand; re-run instead.\n\n### Set up\n1. Set `baseUrl` (default `http://127.0.0.1:8600`) and `datasource`.\n2. Auth headers are **disabled by default**, matching `auth.enabled: false`. Enable `x-client-cert-subject` (mesh identity) or `Authorization` (token) once the deployment turns auth on.\n3. The trusted raw-SQL folder only works when `api.enable_raw_sql: true`; otherwise those routes are not registered at all and return 404.\n\n`curls/CURLS.md` has the same requests as copy-paste curl, plus the SQL needed to create the demo objects.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8600"
    },
    {
      "key": "datasource",
      "value": "tsdb"
    },
    {
      "key": "channel",
      "value": "orders_changed"
    },
    {
      "key": "callerSubject",
      "value": "orders-api"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 \u00b7 Governed invocation (recommended)",
      "description": "Name a database object and pass parameters. **No SQL crosses the wire**, so there is no injection surface and no arbitrary-table access.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "view",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Request-Id",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-client-cert-subject",
                "value": "{{callerSubject}}",
                "disabled": true
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{apiKey}}",
                "disabled": true
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/datasources/{{datasource}}/view",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "datasources",
                "{{datasource}}",
                "view"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Query a view or table by name with structured filters\n\nAuthorized as `read` on the data source.",
